															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/elogee-fishtruck" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4037075); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4037075&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606834515" alt="Elogee FishTruck" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4037075)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/elogee-fishtruck" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4037075); return false;" >Elogee FishTruck</a></span> <span class="odate time_1555339479 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">15 Apr 2019 14:44</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4219776">
									

<p>I know you said this wasn't too important, but I'd like to break down the story told in these two possible iterations of the document. There are two immediately noticeable narratives: the quarter narrative and the nickel narrative</p>
<p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Nickel:</span></strong></p>
<ul>
<li>An <em>anomalous item</em> (nickel) becomes officially designated after <em>Janitor Rodriguez</em> inadvertently discovers its extra effect, Rodriguez gets promoted to researcher in the process</li>
<li>An unnamed subject (who we can assume is Rodriguez) tests with the nickel and creates a new <em>anomalous item</em> (previously <em>non-anomalous</em> quarter) in the process</li>
<li><em>Rogers</em> conducts rest of testing and neutralizes the nickel in the process, making the nickel <em>non-anomalous</em></li>
</ul>
<p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Quarter:</span></strong></p>
<ul>
<li>An <em>anomalous item</em> (quarter) becomes officially designated after <em>Janitor Rogers</em> inadvertently discovers its extra effect, Rogers gets promoted to researcher in the process</li>
<li>An unnamed subject (who we can assume is Rogers) tests with the quarter and creates a new <em>anomalous item</em> (previously <em>non-anomalous</em> nickel) in the process</li>
<li><em>Rodriguez</em> conducts rest of testing and neutralizes the quarter in the process, making the quarter <em>non-anomalous</em></li>
</ul>
<p>At first, this doesn't make sense. The quarter can only be made anomalous when the nickel is designated, and vice versa. However, I propose three possible interpretations:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show&nbsp;interpretations</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;interpretations</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<ul>
<li>The documents take place in separate universes. This is the easiest explanation, but also the lamest.</li>
<li>The quarter mentioned in the nickel narrative isn't necessarily the quarter mentioned in the quarter narrative. This, again, is an easy explanation, but a bit lame as well, unless taken to its logical extreme where a <em>lot</em> more nickels and quarters are being made anomalous, designated, and neutralized.</li>
<li>The documents represent a loop. Let's think about this. Part of this is guessing in my part because we don't know who conducted tests 2-5, but here's my reordering of events:
<ul>
<li>Non-anomalous nickel is used in testing of designated quarter, non-anomalous nickel becomes anomalous and is added to LoAO, Researcher Rogers (who I believe is in charge of testing for quarter) is probably demoted, perhaps to a <em>janitor</em> role.</li>
<li>Rodriguez becomes researcher in charge of quarter testing, neutralizes quarter in the process and quarter becomes non-anomalous</li>
<li>Nickel is discovered to be designation worthy, Rodriguez is promoted in the process from janitor to researcher</li>
<li>Now non-anomalous quarter is used in testing of designated nickel, non-anomalous quarter becomes anomalous and is added to LoAO, Researcher Rodriguez (who I believe is in charge of testing for nickel) is probably demoted, perhaps to a <em>janitor role</em></li>
<li>Rogers becomes researcher in charge of nickel testing, neutralizes nickel in the process and nickel becomes non-anomalous</li>
<li>Quarter is discovered to be designation worthy, Rogers is promoted in the process from janitor to researcher.</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Wash, rinse, repeat. It's an endless loop, nickel to quarter, Rigers to Rodriguez, <em>heads to tails</em>.</p>
<p>Hippo, you mad lad. +1</p>

