														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4226881">
									

<p>Very classic SCP feel, but not totally in a positive way. The Director notes saying &quot;Don't do this again&quot; were so common in the early days. It doesn't feel very clinical and formal like the modern Foundation and has roots in the older, sillier days where researchers could take scips home for personal use and project leads could be demoted to D-Class for doing obviously poorly-thought-out tests. It's hammy, and I can almost appreciate it as a throwback, but it doesn't <em>feel</em> like the Foundation at all. The only reasons it's not a downvote are: the fact that the researcher was janitorial staff five minutes ago; and the neat gimmick of a coin-flip deciding which story you read.</p>

